    conjunct paper bundle at the same `N`. -/
theorem baryogenesis_leptogenesis_paper_bundle_inbound
    {N : ℕ} (_hN : sakharov_realised_at_truncation N) :
    (|eta_B_substrate N - baryonPhotonRatio_PDG| < 1e-9) ∧
    (0 < epsilon_sterile_asymmetry) ∧
    (0 < BR_substrate N) ∧
    (Fintype.card SU3ColorChannel = 3 ∧
      Function.Bijective channelToGeneration4 ∧
      channelToGeneration4 .catalan_g = (3 : Fin 4)) :=
  baryogenesis_leptogenesis_paper_bundle N

/-! ## §5.  Inbound bridge #4 — cycle-41+42 three-conjunct
        `matter_asymmetry_and_no_new_physics_paper_bundle`

The cycle-41+42 Ruchbah headline
`matter_asymmetry_and_no_new_physics_paper_bundle` combines, for every
truncation budget `N`, (i) existential CP envelope ratio
`∃ ε ∈ (0,1), |η_B - η_PDG| ≤ ε · η_PDG`, (ii) no-new-physics KATRIN
gap exclusion `∀ m ∈ (1e-5, m_e_eV), ¬ FermionCatalogue.exists_at_mass m`,
(iii) 4-channel bijection with Catalan-G in sterile slot.  The
bridge imports the Sakharov realisation hypothesis and closes the
three-conjunct paper bundle parametric in `N`. -/

/-- **Inbound bridge #4** — Sakharov realisation at `N` ⇒ cycle-41+42
    `matter_asymmetry_and_no_new_physics_paper_bundle` (at the same `N`).

    Ruchbah's headline holds unconditionally for every `N`; the
    bridge realises an APPLIES edge from the Sakharov-realisation
    predicate at truncation budget `N` into the three-conjunct paper
    bundle at the same `N`. -/
theorem matter_asymmetry_and_no_new_physics_paper_bundle_inbound
    {N : ℕ} (_hN : sakharov_realised_at_truncation N) :
    (∃ ε : ℝ,
       0 < ε ∧ ε < 1 ∧
       |eta_B_substrate N - baryonPhotonRatio_PDG|
         ≤ ε * baryonPhotonRatio_PDG) ∧
    (∀ m : ℝ,
       sterile_window_upper < m → m < m_e_eV →
       ¬ FermionCatalogue.exists_at_mass m) ∧
    (Function.Bijective channelToGeneration4 ∧
      channelToGeneration4 .catalan_g = (3 : Fin 4)) :=
  matter_asymmetry_and_no_new_physics_paper_bundle N

